<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Radon in Winnipeg is common, invisible and cheap to check for. It's a radioactive gas that seeps up from the soil and collects in basements, and you can't see it or smell it. Health Canada says radon is the number one cause of lung cancer in non-smokers, linked to more than 3,000 lung cancer deaths in Canada each year. That's worth saying once. After that, the job is practical: test, and fix it if the number comes back high.</p><p>Prairie Radon Co connects Winnipeg homeowners with independent radon professionals for <a href="/radon-testing/">testing</a> and <a href="/radon-mitigation/">mitigation</a>. The honest first step is a long-term test of at least 91 days in the heating season, even though it means you won't need a contractor for a few months. If you already have a result over 200 Bq/m3, call (204) 555-0173 and we'll put you in touch with a mitigation professional who can quote the work.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Winnipeg</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Winnipeg Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Long-term radon testing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A test of at least 91 days in the lowest lived-in level of your Winnipeg home, 30 cm above the floor and away from the sump. The Manitoba government puts kits at between $50 and $100.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Radon mitigation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Sub-slab depressurization: a pipe through the basement floor and a fan that vents soil gas outside. Winnipeg installers advertise systems from about $1,500 to $3,000.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Radon and a home sale</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Buying or selling in Winnipeg and radon has come up in the inspection or the conditions? We'll explain the testing side; the contract questions belong with your realtor or lawyer.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Fan and system checks</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A noisy fan, a dead one, or a manometer that doesn't look right. Health Canada's 2014 national figure for a replacement fan is $200 to $300.</p>
      </div>
</div>
